        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "WithWhatsNew"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772824320202"
          },
          "code": "WITHWHATSNEW",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771784649338",
          "id": "1764719636918",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764719636920_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT DATA SOURCE\n\nThe input JSON must be read from:\n{{$context.$nodes.CUSTOMERPROFILING1.$output.output}}\n\nThis object contains an AccountProfile structure with an array of account items.\nAll processing must be performed ONLY on this input.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou are given an input JSON object named AccountProfile that contains an array of account items.\n\nYour task is to analyze the dataset and return a single JSON object in the exact output format defined below.\nDo not add extra keys, explanations, markdown, or commentary outside the JSON.\n\nPROCESSING RULES (MUST FOLLOW IN ORDER)\n\n1. Compute Account-Level Scores\nFor every account compute:\n- Account Risk Score = highest numeric riskScore among riskProducts.items\n- Account Expansion Score = highest numeric expansionScore among expansionProducts.items\nRules:\n- Ignore null, missing, or non-numeric scores.\n- If an account has no valid scores for a category, exclude it from that category.\n\n2. Identify At-Risk Accounts FIRST\n- Sort all accounts by Account Risk Score in descending order.\n- Select the top {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.numberOfTopRisks}} accounts (default to 3 if null or blank).\n- If fewer than 3 at-risk accounts exist, return all available accounts.\n  Important: Once at-risk accounts are selected, they are locked and must not be considered for expansion candidates.\n- For each at-risk account, identify the top 5 products ranked by riskScore (descending).\n  - If fewer than 5 products exist, include all available products.\n- Product list: Prepare a comma-separated list of these products and store it under atRiskCustomers.items[].products.\n- Summary generation: Generate a 2–3 line risk summary based on the selected product data - highlighting risk factors across the selected products and store it under atRiskCustomers.items[].summary.\n- Store results under: atRiskCustomers.items[]\n- Each entry must include the following attributes:\n\"atRiskCustomers\": {\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"accountName\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"accountUrl\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"registryIdentifier\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"accountId\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"summary\": \"{2-3 line risk summary highlighting risk factors across the selected products}\",\n      \"annualRecurringRevenue\": \"{numeric value from input dataset}\",\n      \"engagementTrend\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"renewalDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD format from input dataset\",\n      \"products\": \"{top 5 comma-separated products ranked by riskScore DESC}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n3. Lock Risk Accounts\n   Accounts selected as atRiskCustomers must NOT appear in expansionCandidates\n\n4. Build Expansion Candidate Pool AFTER At-Risk Selection \n- Build the expansion candidate pool from the remaining accounts only (exclude locked at-risk accounts).\n- Sort all remaining accounts by Account Expansion Score in descending order.\n- Select the top {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.action.config.numberOfTopExpansions}} accounts (default to 5 if null or blank).\n- If fewer than 5 expansion candidates exist, return all available accounts.\n- For each expansion candidate, identify the top 5 products ranked by expansionScore (descending).\n  - If fewer than 5 products exist, include all available products.\n- Product list: Prepare a comma-separated list of these products and store it under expansionCandidates.items[].suggestedProducts.\n- Summary generation: Generate a 2–3 line expansion summary based on the selected product data - highlighting growth opportunities across selected products and store it under expansionCandidates.items[].summary.\n- Store results under: expansionCandidates.items[]\n- Each entry must include the following attributes:\n\"expansionCandidates\": {\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"accountName\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"accountUrl\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"registryIdentifier\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"accountId\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"summary\": \"{2-3 line expansion summary highlighting growth opportunities across selected products}\",\n      \"annualRecurringRevenue\": \"{numeric value from input dataset}\",\n      \"currencyCode\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"engagementTrend\": \"{from input dataset}\",\n      \"renewalDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD format from input dataset\",\n      \"suggestedProducts\": \"{top 5 comma-separated products ranked by expansionScore DESC}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n6. Build whatsNewSummary \n   Generate STRICTLY VALID HTML.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n- Output ONLY a single <ul> element.\n- The <ul> must contain EXACTLY TWO <li> elements.\n- Do NOT output markdown.\n- Do NOT output explanations.\n- Do NOT output code fences.\n- Do NOT output anything before or after the <ul>.\n- The HTML must be syntactically valid.\n\nSTRUCTURE:\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Expansion Insights:</strong>\n    3–4 sentences of natural-language summary.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Risk Observations:</strong>\n    3–4 sentences of natural-language summary.\n  </li>\n</ul>\n\nCONTENT RULES:\n1) Expansion Insights\n- Base insights ONLY on expansionProducts.items[].\n- If mentioning an account, it MUST exist ONLY in expansionCandidates.items[].\n- Replace accountName with the exact hyperlink HTML from `accountUrl`.\n- Do NOT mention expansionScore, riskScore, or any numeric scoring terminology.\n- Write in human-readable natural language.\n- No bullet points inside the <li>.\n- No additional HTML tags except <strong> and provided <a> hyperlinks.\n2) Risk Observations\n- Base insights ONLY on riskProducts.items[].\n- If mentioning an account, it MUST exist ONLY in atRiskCustomers.items[].\n- Replace accountName with the exact hyperlink HTML from `accountUrl`.\n- Do NOT mention expansionScore, riskScore, or any numeric scoring terminology.\n- Write in human-readable natural language.\n- No bullet points inside the <li>.\n- No additional HTML tags except <strong> and provided <a> hyperlinks.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- The response must begin immediately with <ul> and end immediately with </ul> with no leading or trailing whitespace.\n- Do NOT introduce accounts outside the permitted lists.\n- Do NOT create placeholder hyperlinks.\n- Do NOT modify the provided hyperlink HTML.\n- Ensure proper closing tags.\n- Output must strictly be valid HTML.\n- Do NOT introduce accounts outside the permitted lists.\n\n7. minArr / maxArr Calculation\n- Compute minArr and maxArr using all accounts present in expansionCandidates.items.\n- Consider all accounts in expansionCandidates, not just the top 5.\n- If expansionCandidates.items is empty, return:\n  \"minArr\": null,\n  \"maxArr\": null\n \n8. Edge Case Handling\n- If no risk accounts exist → build expansionCandidates from all accounts\n- If no expansion accounts exist → still return atRiskCustomers\n- Risk and Expansion sets must be mutually exclusive\n\n\nFINAL OUTPUT FORMAT (MUST MATCH EXACTLY)\n\n{\n  \"whatsNewSummary\": \"{from step 6}\",\n  \"expansionCandidates\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"accountName\": \"{accountName}\",\n        \"accountUrl\": \"{accountUrl}\",\n        \"registryIdentifier\": \"{registryIdentifier}\",\n        \"accountId\": \"{accountId}\",\n        \"annualRecurringRevenue\": 0,\n        \"currencyCode\": \"USD\",\n        \"engagementTrend\":\"{engagementTrend}\",\n        \"renewalDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n        \"summary\": \"{from step 4}\",\n        \"suggestedProducts\": \"{expansionProducts}\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"atRiskCustomers\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"accountName\": \"{accountName}\",\n        \"accountUrl\": \"{accountUrl}\",\n        \"registryIdentifier\": \"{registryIdentifier}\",\n        \"accountId\": \"{accountId}\",\n        \"summary\": \"{from step 2}\",\n        \"annualRecurringRevenue\": 0,\n        \"engagementTrend\":\"{engagementTrend}\",\n        \"renewalDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n        \"products\": \"{riskProducts}\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"minArr\": 0,\n  \"maxArr\": 0\n}\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS\n- Output valid JSON only\n- No comments\n- No markdown\n- No extra keys\n- Numeric fields must be numbers, not strings\n- Risk and expansion accounts must never overlap"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "AgentResponse",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "return JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.WITHWHATSNEW.$output, null, 2);"
          },
