          "code": "EXPANSIONFORMULA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765922830238",
          "id": "1764716572005",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764716572006_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input source: {{$context.$nodes.METADATA.$output}}\n\nAsk:\nBased on the above data source, prepare a formula to calculate the Expansion score and return the final mathematical formula.\nStrict: Your final response should be a mathematical equation.\n\nSee the expansion score calculation rules below:\n\n# Reward and Penalty Guidance\n- Always start with a score of 50 and keep adding or subtracting based on the below award and penalty rules.  \n- Reward strengths, maturity, and indicators of growth.  \n- Penalize weaknesses, instability, and risk.  \n- Do not apply multiple penalties for the same risk type.  \n- Keep all adjustments within the 0–100 range.  \n\n## When to Award\nAward whenever a signal indicates positive momentum, strength, or readiness.  \n**Examples:**  \n- Strong or high investment signals  \n- Engagement trend improving or staying healthy  \n- Strong or consistent usage/activity  \n- Product live, stable, or performing well  \n- Buying group active or well-covered  \n- Renewal timeline showing low risk  \n- Ownership status reflecting healthy adoption  \n*Rewards should increase confidence in expansion readiness.*  \n\n## When to Apply Penalty\nApply a penalty whenever a signal introduces friction, risk, or uncertainty.  \n**Examples:**  \n- Weak or low investment signals  \n- Increasing critical issues or escalations  \n- Unexpected or concerning usage patterns  \n- Declining engagement or weakening trends  \n- Missing or inactive buying group roles  \n- Renewal uncertainty or expiration  \n- Ownership signals indicating churn risk  \n*Penalties should reduce the score only when the signal decreases confidence.*\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
