              "id": "1764716720766_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input sources:\n1.) Input metadata => {{$context.$nodes.METADATA.$output}} \n\nAsk:\nBased on the above data source, prepare a formula to calculate the Risk score and return the final mathematical formula.\nStrict: Your final response should be a mathematical equation.\n\nSee the risk score calculation rules below:\n\n# Reward and Penalty Guidance\n\n## When to Award (Increase Risk Score)\nAward a higher risk score whenever a signal indicates exposure, vulnerability, or instability.  \n**Examples:**  \n- Weak or declining investment trends  \n- Low or inconsistent usage  \n- Product stability or adoption issues  \n- Renewal or ownership uncertainties  \n- Gaps in engagement or inactive buying groups  \n\n## When to Apply Penalty (Reduce Risk Score)\nReduce risk score if a product shows signs of stability, adoption, or healthy usage.  \n**Examples:**  \n- Strong or consistent engagement  \n- Stable usage and performance  \n- Low churn signals  \n- Healthy renewal timeline  \n\n## General Principles\n- Reward indicators of risk, weakness, or potential churn.  \n- Penalize signals of strength or stability.  \n- Keep all adjustments within the 0–100 range.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
